plicit) resolver (same explicit > REBAR_ROOT > git precedence), preserving each caller's not-found handling (_init exits 1; init -> None)'","_config_sources.repo_root L40-51 falls through to 'return Path.cwd()' after git fails -- no not-found signal","_cli/_init.py L50-57: root=os.environ.get('REBAR_ROOT') or _git_toplevel(); if not root: raise SystemExit(1) -- no cwd fallback","_commands/init.py L184-195: returns None when git rev-parse fails -- no cwd fallback"],"finding":"The REBAR_ROOT cut targets an OWNED resolver (config.repo_root / _config_sources.repo_root) whose precedence ends in a Path.cwd() fallback and never signals 'not found', yet the plan requires preserving each caller's not-found handling (_init exits 1; init -> None). Both current callers stop at git (no cwd fallback) precisely so they can detect the not-found case; routing through repo_root() as-is would silently return cwd instead, a behavior change the plan does not resolve.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffb87786749a43a2e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Cut targets -> '2 REBAR_ROOT' bullet","norm_id":"n9b53dbfbb6ff20f7","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["rebar init / _init invoked outside a git repo with REBAR_ROOT unset: today exits 1 / returns None; after routing through repo_root() would silently proceed with cwd as root"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":